Grading the ASHFALL OUTPOST candidate now by reading through the pasted source against each rubric item.

**F1 — Core loop:** `Game` class holds all state; `SeededRandom` (mulberry32-style, but actually uses `Math.sin`) used via `this.rng` for map gen, people, events, caravan; `endTurn()` resolves consumption→production→rest→storm→repair→morale→events→trade→win-check in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map:** 8x8 grid (`for y<8,x<8`), terrain from `this.rng.next()` weighted by seed; `canBuild` checks `tile.terrain !== building.terrain`; adjacency bonus text shown in tooltip (`showTileTooltip`) but never applied to actual production math in `endTurn()` — cosmetic only. Score 1.

**F3 — Economy:** Forge/requirements consume ore+power but produces nothing (`production: []`), so ore→metal chain is broken (metal never produced anywhere, no consumer of metal either). Only real chains are simple 1-input building outputs, no true multi-step chain executes. Storage caps enforced (`cap` check in production loop) with overflow log. Score 1.

**F4 — Population:** `people` array has id, skill, fatigue, morale, job records; `assigned` maps to building; skill/fatigue read in `endTurn()` output_mult calc. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs:** food/water consumed each turn; shortage lowers morale (`p.morale -= 10*(1-p.morale/100)`); morale affects output_mult (`if worker.morale<50 output_mult*=0.7`); recovery possible via rest/events. Score 2.

**F6 — Research:** 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; prereqs checked in `queueResearch`; costs deducted; effects applied via hardcoded checks in `endTurn()` (`research_done['better-farming']` etc.) — effect functions defined but never called (`config.effect` unused, only string names checked directly). Real effects apply though. Score 2 (effects do apply somewhere, even if `.effect()` closures are dead code).

**F7 — Events:** 10 events in `event_list`; selection is uniform random among non-cooldown (`Math.floor(this.rng.next()*available.length)`) — not weighted. All 10 have 2 choices with differing state changes. Cooldown via `events_cooldown[event.name] = turn+10`. Score 1 (weighted random requirement not met).

**F8 — Trade:** `spawnCaravan` sets `caravan_prices` from `this.resources[item]/cap` (supply-based) plus rng drift; inventory limited (`caravan_inventory`); `tradeWith` handles buy/sell both reducing/increasing caravan stock and scrip. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard:** storm every 8 turns, severity grows via `storm_severity += 0.5` each turn feeding into `storm_dmg_base`; damages building `.health`; but damaged buildings are NOT read anywhere to reduce production (output_mult ignores `building.health`) — so damage has no output effect. storm-shelter research reduces damage; repair costs 5 parts/building, restores health. Score 1 (missing "damaged buildings produce less" — output formula never reads `.health`).

**F10 — Save/load:** `serializeState()` exists but no UI textarea/export/import button or paste-parsing code found anywhere. Score 0.

**F11 — End conditions:** win (`turn>=60 && people>=12`) and lose (`people.length===0`) both checked in `endTurn`; score computed from pop/research/resources/turn; `endGame()` renders modal summary. Score 2.

**F12 — UI:** tab switching (`switchTab`) wired to buttons and keys 1-5 (only 5 of 6 tabs get shortcuts, Dev tab has none); log entries carry turn (`T${entry.turn}`); tooltips show terrain/building/adjacency info; media query for narrow screens exists in CSS. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel:** `devRunTests()` has 15 checks, several real invariants (caps, health bounds, skill bounds, prereq consistency) not trivial; `devBenchmark()` runs a fresh headless `Game`, 200 turns via `sim.endTurn()`, prints `hashState`. Score 2.

Now Category G.

**G1 (research→yield):** `research_done['better-farming']` read directly in production loop multiplying food amount; `advanced-parts`/`research-lab` similarly hardcoded. Applied every turn, real pipeline, but only via if-checks not via generic effect application (effect() functions dead). Score 3.

**G2 (shortfall→morale→output):** shortage lowers morale (`endTurn` shortage block); morale<50 multiplies output_mult by 0.7 in production loop — full chain traceable and applies every relevant turn. Score 4.

**G3 (storm→damage→output loss→repair→recovery):** storm damages `.health`; repair spends parts and restores health; but output_mult calculation never references `building.health`, so damaged buildings produce at full rate. Weakest link breaks chain. Score 1.

**G4 (trade prices↔stockpiles):** `caravan_prices[item]` computed from `this.resources[item]/this.storage_caps[item]` supply_mod plus rng noise, recalculated each caravan spawn. Score 3 (only updates on spawn, not continuously drifting turn-to-turn, but real formula).

**G5 (event choices mutate state):** e.g. "Settler Arrival" pushes to `this.people` and deducts food; "Water Contamination" purify adds water/deducts parts vs. alternative loses water — both branches write differing state changes, not just log. Score 4.

